// An opaque rounded fill for a box whose WIDTH springs by `-exact-layout-transition`, drawn so no
// filled box ever resizes. While a layout transition resizes a box, the iOS host paints it on a
// surface layer that keeps Core Animation's corner only in some cases (exact2 Surface.swift
// paintSurface; parity-tools/exact-issues/radius-reduced.md): the phone showed square or
// re-curved corners for the whole spring (composable-text, 2026-11-15).
//
// Two clips of a fixed width, `half`, each holding a long pill of the colour and radius: one
// pinned to the box's left edge (it rides the box's own layout offset), one to its right edge
// (its own layout transition, the box's spring, moves it as the edge moves). Neither resizes,
// so both keep the layer's own corner; they overlap in the middle (an opaque colour: the overlap
// does not show). `half` must be at least half the widest box and at most the narrowest, or
// a clip shows past the far end. The box: `position="relative"`, this as its first child, the
// height fixed for the spring (only the width moves).

component PillFill
  props
    color: string
    radius: number
    half: number
    // The box's own -exact-layout-transition.
    spring: string
  view
    view position="absolute" left=0 top=0 bottom=0 width=half overflow="hidden"
      pointer-events="none" aria-hidden=true
      view position="absolute" left=0 top=0 bottom=0 width=2000 background-color=color
        border-radius=radius corner-shape="-exact-continuous"
    view position="absolute" right=0 top=0 bottom=0 width=half overflow="hidden"
      pointer-events="none" aria-hidden=true -exact-layout-transition=spring
      view position="absolute" right=0 top=0 bottom=0 width=2000 background-color=color
        border-radius=radius corner-shape="-exact-continuous"
